## Summary

The evaluator's feedback was that the lift measurement logic was correctly and backward-compatibly implemented, but the two required unit tests were missing since the only existing lift-related test hand-constructed a hard-coded AccuracyStats rather than exercising the actual aggregation.

I completed the missing test work:

**`src/commands_risk.rs`** — added `test_replay_validate_core_persists_lift_measurement`:
• Constructs a broke set that hits 2 predicted files (hits), 1 non-predicted scored file (scored surprise), and non-scored churn (`docs/notes.md, DAY_COUNT`).
• Asserts total_scored = `all_ranked.len()` (7) and scored_broke = 3 (hits + scored surprises, excluding non-source churn) are persisted on the event JSON.
• Verifies the lift computed from the persisted event is a plausible number (>1, since flagged files break more often than baseline).

**`src/commands_risk_accuracy.rs`** — added two tests:
• `test_compute_accuracy_stats_lift_aggregation_mixed_events`: a mix of old-format events (no lift fields) and lift-carrying events. Confirms absent-field events are skipped without panic and the pooled lift is aggregated correctly (computed expected value 1.2 exactly).
• `test_compute_accuracy_stats_lift_no_fields_is_none`: when no event carries the lift fields, `overall_lift is None` and the report renders "—".

I also fixed a pre-existing clippy warning (`single_match) in the compute_accuracy_stats` aggregation loop, converting the match to an if let per clippy's suggestion, so that `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.

All checks pass: `cargo fmt -- --check, cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`, cargo build, and cargo test (88 passed, 0 failed). No pre-existing tests were removed, and no previously-recorded JSONL events are touched.
